  "notes": [
   "The booklet has no parts-list pages with element IDs for this set, so piece identities are inferred from the pictures and mapped to the closest catalogue types. Colours are in props and may not match the catalogue name (for example the white 1x8 plate is typed lego-346026, and the black rotor blades are typed lego-4189400).",
   "Steps 1-5 (the chassis) are ambiguous. I modelled it as two black wheel holders bridged by a light grey 2x2 plate, a light grey wheel holder on top, and a white 2x4 plate on top of that.",
   "Step 6 (dark blue bricks) has no parts box. I assumed one 1x4, one 2x2 and one 1x2 dark blue brick.",
   "Step 11 (white cab pieces) and step 12 (aqua pieces) are also inferred, and the step 12 aqua pieces are not modelled separately. Stud port assignments are approximate, and several pieces share the same studs.",
   "Part 2 in step 10 is two trans-yellow round plates on a clip plate. Both round plates are joined to the clip plate's single catalogue stud port, so the port is shared.",
   "The fuel tank floats are modelled as two yellow round 2x2 bricks plus a dome. Each tank is joined to the pins of both black wheel holders. The tank's pin-hole port is null because the catalogue type has none.",
   "The pilot minifig appears first in step 16, so I added it there. Its helmet is joined to the head's 'top' port."
  ]
 },
